{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/896035-ideas-on-the-use-of-abyssals-in-ex3","id":896035,"title":"Ideas on the use of Abyssals in Ex3","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-22T05:58:45-07:00","id":896035,"title":"Ideas on the use of Abyssals in Ex3","content":"In a game I'm running, the PCs have unintentionally inherited something of great value to a deathlord. Naturally, a circle of abyssals will be coming after them. I decided to go with Abyssals as antagonists because there is frankly more mechanical support for them in Ex3 than anything but other Solars. I don't have the time or the expertise to write entire Terrestrial, Lunar, Sidereal, or Spirit charm sets, but I can basically just tweak some solar charms for a different feel and I'm good to go with Abyssals.<br /> <br /> I don't want to run them as 2e Abyssals, however. That is, I don't want them to exist exclusively as extensions of a deathlord's will. I want them to be cool in their own right, but that got me wondering a bit. The devs have said that Abyssals will have a lot more options this time around, and that even those working for a deathlord will have not have such an obnoxious mechanic to deal with as resonance the way it worked before, or, &quot;your deathlord snaps his fingers from worlds away and you die.&quot;<br /> <br /> I like the idea of these guys being beholden to a deathlord, but I'm having trouble coming up with a good way to handle that. Should deathlords still have monstrances that let them contain and offer exaltations to dying heroes? Should this still give them some measure of supernatural influence? Or should Abyssals come about like Solars (more spontaneously), and then many are drawn to the willing service of deathlords somehow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9749-andrew-d","name":"Andrew D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T07:38:32-07:00","id":896078,"title":"","content":"I'll chip in with something after my game session. Remind me later if I haven't said anything by like tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T08:21:51-07:00","id":896095,"title":"","content":"I would suggest keeping the scene where the Deathlord makes an offer to a dying person for Exaltation. It's very iconic and pretty cool. I would just as soon get rid of the idea of the monstrance however and the idea that the Deathlord has magical powers over the life and death of the Abyssal (though some Deathlords might lie and claim they do, and others might have Charms, Sorcery or are powerful enough that, if they wanted to, they <i>could</i> potentially kill their errant Deathknight, though it would take more work than a snap of the ).<br /> <br /> I think the specifics would be down to each Deathlord. So some, like the Lover or the Mask of Winters or the Silver Prince might rule more through giving their Deathknights praise, honours and rewards (basically enticing them through their greed and egos) others might use a bit more fear (like the FaFL or the Dowager) and some might keep their knights in line through other means (the Bishop likely uses a bit of brainwashing and religious indoctrination). <br /> <br /> Basically though it should be clear that a given deathknight has a personal relationship with her Deathlord and chooses to remain in service. And, importantly, if the Abyssal decides otherwise, there aren't any magical chains forcing her to stay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T09:01:49-07:00","id":896105,"title":"","content":"charms honestly don't matter for QC...you can literally do whatever you want, with the combat system fairly standardized Lunars, Spirits, Demons etc...you can literally make them in 10 min to half a hour at most.<br /> <br /> But anyway for abyssals, just make as suggested by anubis deathknights following the chivalry of death and essentially associating to a deathlord...I still have the abyssal kickstarter preview that they did have in 2013...they had associated some powers with the deathlords, not sure if it is still the case, but this actually even easier and more fun when making your deathknight, as they would get powers related to their deathlord of choice.<br /> <br /> edit: guess a good way to see Abyssals...would be like master/apprentice. Some death knights can still rebel, as they don't have the leash of master/slave of 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2127,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","user":"Eltacolibre","date":". 05-22-2016, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T09:32:45-07:00","id":896113,"title":"","content":"Laws, was that an actual thing in 2E? Abyssals being mere extensions of their Deathlord's will? Deathknights dying when their liege snaps his fingers a continent away? Or some less hyperbolic version of the above? I recall plenty of Abyssals being &quot;cool in their own right&quot; in my 2E game. I ask because I tend to go through books as if editing a script for performance and just mentally black out stuff I think is dumb and never think of it again. So was this really how it was? And only in 2E? I recall Deathlords having power over their knights since 1E.<br /> <br /> To answer the actual question: Yes, most Abyssals should be the willing vassals of the Deathlords, who act as the distributors of the Black Exaltation. Deathlords should be able to use monstrances to discipline their charges in some way, but not to effortlessly kill them. This is more compelling for several reasons.<br /> <br /> 1. Uniqueness. The more we can do to avoid &quot;goth solars,&quot; the happier everyone shall be<br /> 2. Gives the Deathlords power and agency as arc villains and overlords<br /> 3. Creates a dynamic where the Deathords have a tiger by the tail<br /> 4. Makes rebel or unaffiliated Deathknights more special<br /> 5. Lets you play with the feudal lord/knight relationship which suits the Abyssals gothic themes<br /> <br /> So, do give Deathlords some authority over most Abyssals, but not enough to eliminate the DKs\u2019 individuality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11816,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","user":"Foxcalibur","date":". 05-22-2016, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T09:51:49-07:00","id":896123,"title":"","content":"My view on the subject: ghosts. Ghosts, ghosts, ghosts, ghosts.<br /> <br /> Maybe there's a technique that conjures up a sickly blue flame that separates separate mortal souls from mortal bodies, sending them directly to the Underworld. Maybe the Abyssal may throw that flame directly at you to burn your own soul, still trapped in its prison of flesh. Maybe the Abyssal may call upon the hosts of cursed dead that they sent to the Underworld prematurely, sending them at you and detonating their ectoplasm. Or even eating those ghosts, building a pyre within themselves, and then setting it aflame to draw Essence and power from that conflagration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T10:34:53-07:00","id":896148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foxcalibur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/896035-ideas-on-the-use-of-abyssals-in-ex3?p=896113#post896113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Laws, was that an actual thing in 2E? Abyssals being mere extensions of their Deathlord's will? Deathknights dying when their liege snaps his fingers a continent away? Or some less hyperbolic version of the above? I recall plenty of Abyssals being &quot;cool in their own right&quot; in my 2E game. I ask because I tend to go through books as if editing a script for performance and just mentally black out stuff I think is dumb and never think of it again. So was this really how it was? And only in 2E? I recall Deathlords having power over their knights since 1E.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a very ill-advised passage in the 1e Abyssals book about this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted: The Abyssals</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deathknights who have time and time again proven their opposition to the cause of Oblivion, despite black miracles and other punishments, earn nothing less than death. Her Deathlord master hurls her Monstrance of Celestial Portion into the Mouth of the Void, destroying the deathknight forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>This concept also made it into 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoEP: Abyssals</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the worst-case scenarios, however, a Deathlord can deliver a punishment whence there is no return and no hope of forgiveness. If a deathknight truly enrages his master, the Deathlord can hurl the doomed failure\u2019s Monstrance of Celestial Portion into the Abyss, destroying the deathknight utterly, Exaltation and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>This had undesirable implications for the status of Abyssals as free agents. I do not expect it to return. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T10:43:04-07:00","id":896153,"title":"","content":"Something I once did with a custom made Deathlord was that she had a Black Tome that sealed oaths much like an Eclipse caste and she would grant people wishes in exchange for their souls. The catch was that she would let them live for a number of years based on their race or exaltation life expectancy. She would extend this time period for those that proved useful to her and shorten it for failure. However, eventually she would claim the persons soul and use it for Soulsteel. She was a little quirky as well. No one was allowed to be unhappy in her shadowland. After all everyone that lived there had been granted their lives greatest wish. Well as long as it was within her powers to pull off and subject to interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4498-ardis","name":"Ardis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T10:56:57-07:00","id":896162,"title":"","content":"Oh yeeeeeeeah! Duh! Monstrance-chucking. I remember now.<br /> <br /> I mean, on the one hand, I think that's a powerful bit of leverage to give your Evil Overlord, and a cool plot hook: If you want to be a free Abyssal, go steal your monstrance. This is makes for a very dramatic narrative, but is the sort of thing Bad Storytellers will ruin every time. &quot;Oh shit! You've gone off the rails! Um... uh... your Deathlord hurls your monstrance! You're dead!&quot;<br /> <br /> In my own campaign I have it so hurling a monstrance containing an Abyssal Exaltation into the void destroys the monstrance, but the Exaltation itself is already infused with voidstuff, and just tethers back to its deathknighr, effectively freeing him to be the avatar of entropy he was made to be. Otherwise, Deathlords can use the Monstrance as a very powerful focus through which to cast sympathetic magic at their deathknights for good or ill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T11:18:21-07:00","id":896176,"title":"","content":"Funily enough, the Scroll of Errata went a similar way @Foxcalibur:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Scroll of Errata PG 53</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Destroying a Monsterance<br /> of Celestial Portion</b><br /> Though some Deathlords attempt to control their servants with tales of Exalts\u2019 souls held hostage in their Monstrances, such threats are hollow lies. If an Abyssal\u2019s Monstrance is de- stroyed, the only repercussion for the Exalt is a sudden feeling of hope that replenishes all her Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T11:38:53-07:00","id":896189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/896035-ideas-on-the-use-of-abyssals-in-ex3?p=896176#post896176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funily enough, the Scroll of Errata went a similar way @Foxcalibur:</div> </div> </div> </div>All things serve the Beam, it seems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:44:57-07:00","id":896279,"title":"","content":"I seem to remember somewhere that deathlords could cast sorceries or charms on monstrances, or expend willpower or motes to injure abyssals remotely or drain them of willpower. I could be wrong of course, but details aside, the vibe I got from 2e was, &quot;you can totally play a renegade/solo/whatever abyssal because it's cool, and by the way here are a thousand mechanical reasons that it's virtually impossible and no fun at all.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyway!<br /> <br /> I really like the idea of having the different deathlords manage their abyssals' with personalized carrots and sticks. I'll definitely use something like that, and I agree that having them offer the exaltation at the moment of death is a really cool concept that should be held onto.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9749-andrew-d","name":"Andrew D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T23:56:52-07:00","id":896588,"title":"","content":"Destroying Monstrance never had any negative effects on Abyssal in question in 2nd Edition - &quot;Abyssals feel the destruction of their Monstrances as a breath of hope, regaining all Willpower points&quot; (Manual of Exalted Powers - Abyssals). All the stories about destroying it and killing Abyssal in question were Deathlords' lies since day one. Errata stated that because there were probably some misunderstanding between writers, as in Chapter One (Chosen of the Void) was talking about Monstrance as if throwing it into Mouth of Oblivion would still kill an Abyssal instantly. Well, lesser evil than Infernal first chapters, but still not good.<br /> <br /> It could however be used as supercharged Arcane Link (so destroying it was kinda helpful for rogue Abyssals), while directly telling ST to avoid killing players this way: &quot;Arcane Link: Certain Abyssal Charms (and all necromancy spells) treat a deathknight\u2019s Monstrance as if it were a physical extension of her body, transmitting the effects of the magic directly to her. Deathlords use this dread mystical correspondence to communicate with and punish their deathknights, and to appear in visions to candidates who have not yet chosen whether to die or accept Exaltation. If such effects kill an Abyssal, the cage shatters and the freed Exaltation must be summoned to a new Monstrance. The possibility that another Deathlord might poach the Exaltation, however, usually deters such extreme solutions to treachery.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T00:05:49-07:00","id":896592,"title":"","content":"IIRC the Deathlords <i>told</i> the Abyssals they could kill them by destroying the Monstrances, to keep them in line. I imagine some of the Deathlords in 3e might still take a similar tack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:21:02-07:00","id":896784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andrew D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/896035-ideas-on-the-use-of-abyssals-in-ex3#post896035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the idea of these guys being beholden to a deathlord, but I'm having trouble coming up with a good way to handle that. Should deathlords still have monstrances that let them contain and offer exaltations to dying heroes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssals are Chosen by the Deathlords; the mortal just has to agree when they are on the brink of death.<br /> <br /> As for the nature of the relationship, that's pretty simple. Why does any person in our world choose to &quot;serve&quot; another? Most people don't work for themselves, they work for other people in corporations. Most humans don't spend their time fighting for 100% independence from government, they either accept the government they have, or they try to reform it.<br /> <br /> Deathknights will serve Deathlords for the same reasons people create hierarchies. Serving gains the Deathknight resources (arms and armor, armies, a Manse, etc). Serving gives the Deathknight protection in the form of their master's wrath. Finally, a Deathlord is a mentor for the Deathknight.<br /> <br /> A standard part of Killfuck Soulshitter Syndrome is for all PCs to be 100% independent with nobody having any authority over them. That &quot;feels&quot; right to them, but it's not realistic. When you consciously move away from that construct (and discard the Monstrance nonsense), you remember that normal human behavior is working together and forming a hierarchy, and even Abyssals are still mentally human (even if they are dead).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T09:52:44-07:00","id":896886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andrew D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/896035-ideas-on-the-use-of-abyssals-in-ex3#post896035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of these guys being beholden to a deathlord, but I'm having trouble coming up with a good way to handle that. Should deathlords still have monstrances that let them contain and offer exaltations to dying heroes? Should this still give them some measure of supernatural influence? Or should Abyssals come about like Solars (more spontaneously), and then many are drawn to the willing service of deathlords somehow?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's always genuine honor and gratitude. If you keep the &quot;cusp of death&quot; Exaltation, the Abyssal literally exists because of the Deathlord. Some will feel honor-bound to keep their word and serve the Deathlord, while others may simply feel desperately grateful for their chance at a second life. Obviously, Killfuck Soulshitter wouldn't feel this way, but Exalts with any conscience at all might be torn between loyal service to the man(woman/thing) that saved their life and to whom they swore an oath, and the atrocities they are expected to commit. Can make for some fun RP scenes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T14:31:28-07:00","id":897193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/896035-ideas-on-the-use-of-abyssals-in-ex3?p=896886#post896886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's always genuine honor and gratitude. If you keep the &quot;cusp of death&quot; Exaltation, the Abyssal literally exists because of the Deathlord. Some will feel honor-bound to keep their word and serve the Deathlord, while others may simply feel desperately grateful for their chance at a second life. Obviously, Killfuck Soulshitter wouldn't feel this way, but Exalts with any conscience at all might be torn between loyal service to the man(woman/thing) that saved their life and to whom they swore an oath, and the atrocities they are expected to commit. Can make for some fun RP scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also depends on Deathlord in question - first edition Silver Prince for example seemed almost like genuinely nice guy, but with kinda strange moral compass / strange society focus - he was in my opinion perfect for Deathlord than some players would find interesting to serve (yes, I still hate his &quot;lies, lies, fleet of doom&quot; portrayal from second edition). The Eye was also not bad - pretty much &quot;let me have my toys and go do your job&quot; type of boss.<br /> Some of them however were written as pretty much impossible to stand for someone with conscience - Mask, Dowager and Lover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}